==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|scrutny}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|scrutiny}}, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|scrūtinium||a search, an inquiry}}, from {{etyl|VL.|en}} {{m|la|scrūtārī||to search or examine thoroughly}}, of uncertain origin. Possibly from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{m|la|scrūta||rubbish, broken trash}}; or of {{etyl|gem|en}} origin, related to {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|scrūtnung||examination, investigation, inquiry, search}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|scrūtnian}}, {{m|ang|scrūdnian||to examine carefully, scrutinize, consider, investigate}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*skrudōną}}, {{m|gem-pro|*skruþōną||to search, examine}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*skrud-}}, {{m|gem-pro|*skruþ-||to cut}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*(s)kreut-||to cut}}. Compare {{cog|goh|skrodōn}}, {{m|goh|scrutōn}}, {{m|goh|scrutilōn||to research, explore}}, {{cog|goh|scrod||a search, scrutiny}}, {{cog|got|𐌰𐌽𐌳𐌷𐍂𐌿𐍃𐌺𐌰𐌽||to investigate, explore}}, {{cog|ang|scrēadian||to shred, cut up, cut off, peel, pare, prune}}. More at {{l|en|shred}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈskɹuː.tɪ.ni/|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|scru|ti|ny|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-scrutiny.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|scrutinies}}

# Intense [[study]] of someone or something.
#* Milton
#*: Thenceforth I thought thee worth my nearer view / And narrower '''scrutiny'''.
# Thorough [[inspection]] of a situation or a case.
# An [[examination]] of [[catechumen]]s, in the last week of [[Lent]], who were to receive [[baptism]] on [[Easter]] Day.
# A [[ticket]], or little paper [[billet]], on which a [[vote]] is written.
# An examination by a [[committee]] of the votes given at an election, for the purpose of correcting the [[poll]].
#: {{rfquotek|Brande & C}}

